    cmux-tui-core: registry connections keep their hot statements compiled
    
    The daemon compiled every SQLite statement on every call: cmux-tui-core had
    no prepare_cached at all, and the workspace's rusqlite build left the
    statement cache feature off. A sample of agent hook ingress (the ignored
    agent_hook_ingress_throughput_probe) showed statement compilation at about a
    fifth of the daemon's SQLite CPU on that path: 14% of the journal writer,
    33% of the journal fanout reader and 22% of the agent roster reader. Each
    hook runs the same few dozen statements (the journal INSERTs, the topology
    subject CTE, receipt and causation lookups, the hook pending row, the
    roster's kind reads and snapshot write).
    
    Now every registry connection (the read-write one, the read-only readers,
    the in-memory registry) keeps up to 128 compiled statements
    (REGISTRY_STATEMENT_CACHE_CAPACITY, least recently used out first; a
    statement costs a few KiB), and the hot journal, hook and roster statements
    use prepare_cached. rusqlite's `cache` feature is on (adds hashlink 0.11.1,
    rusqlite's own default dependency; hashbrown 0.16.1 was already in the
    graph). A cached statement is reset when it goes back to the cache, so it
    holds no read snapshot or lock between uses.
    
    Nothing on disk changes: same schema, same rows, same transactions. A
    rollback reads the same files.
    
    Test: reused_statements_read_every_later_commit (a long-lived reader and the
    writer run the same statements again after each of six commits and must read
    each commit).
    
    Measured (aws-m4pro-6, load about 25 on 14 cores, so wall time is noise; CPU
    time of agent_hook_ingress_throughput_probe, 2,000 serial + 4,000 concurrent
    hook events, 4 interleaved runs each, median): user+sys 4.56 s -> 3.69 s
    (-19%), user 2.93 s -> 2.10 s (-28%).
    
    Tests on the build host: cmux-tui-core lib suite 4124 passed, 5 failed; the
    same 5 run alone fail the same way on the base test binary (2 fail on both:
    every_app_command_is_decided_for_the_owner_link,
    a_persons_requests_answer_while_busy_sessions_saturate_the_registry) or pass
    on both (3, load-sensitive in the full run).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

